  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 218 AM CST Mon Nov 23 2026\n\nToday a surface ridge of high pressure will build into the area from \nthe Plains states. This will provide copious sunshine however, weak \nmixing will still hold high temperatures in the 40s. This surface \nridge will continue to remain over the area tonight into Tuesday \ncontinuing to keep temperatures cool and conditions dry. This will \nproduce lows tonight in the upper teens to mid 20s. Highs Tuesday, \nwill be the coolest of the week as weak mixing combined with mostly \ncloudy skies as a upper level trough moves through the region holds \nhighs in the upper 30s to lower 40s. The surface ridge continues to \nremain in control Wednesday with a return to partly cloudy \nconditions (at least over the southern CWA) allowing highs to warm a \nfew degrees into the low to mid 40s, despite the continued weak \nmixing. \n\nWednesday night into Thanksgiving Day, a upper level closed low \ntrough will move through the area as a secondary closed upper low \ndevelops over the Gulf coast states. On Thanksgiving, as the closed \nlow that moves through the local area Wednesday night pushes \neastward in the central Mississippi River Valley, the Gulf low \nstarts to lift northeastward along the Appalachians. These two \nfeatures begin to partake in the Fujiwhara effect before the upper \nlow over the Mississippi River Valley moves into the Ohio Valley and \nabsorbs the Appalachian upper low. These features should remain far \nenough east of the area to keep precipitation east of the forecast \narea. Strong northwest flow aloft and weak mixing will hold high \nThanksgiving day in the 40s. Temperatures will warm on Friday as \nupper level flow over the region becomes quasi-zonal and modest WAA \ngets underway. This will lift highs into the upper 40s to mid 50s. \nFriday night into Saturday a progressive trough will move through \nthe region forcing a cold front through the area. Cold air behind \nthis front will be lacking and in fact the modest westerly flow \nbehind the front will allow for deeper mixing pushing highs into the \nlower 50s to near 60. Sunday will bring a return to quasi-zonal flow \naloft over the region will strong WAA at the surface which will aid \nin temperatures again rising into the 50s to lower 60s.",
